# Day 5 — Mechanical Stops and Final Assembly

The final stage focused on adding mechanical stops to control the movement of the retaining rails.

### Work Completed

- Designed cylindrical stop features for the retaining rails
- Positioned the stops near the rail travel limits
- Used assembly mates to determine the correct stop locations
- Designed the stops so the rails cannot rotate excessively past their intended closed positions
- Completed the final mechanical assembly
- Verified the placement of:
  - Main PCB cavity
  - Secondary plate cavity
  - Wiring clearance
  - Wiring passage
  - Retaining rails
  - Rail pivots
  - Mechanical stops

